<section class="features">

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="feature-row__text">
      <p class="feature-row__num">01 &mdash; Strict by default</p>
      <h2 class="feature-row__title">No <code>--strict</code> flag.<br>No gradual mode.<br>No opt-in.</h2>
      <p class="feature-row__body">
        Basilisk treats every untyped function as a type error &mdash; because that&rsquo;s what it is.
        There is no configuration key to make it permissive. The safe path is the only path.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-row__visual">
      <div class="stat-block">
        <span class="stat-block__number">0<span class="stat-block__unit">%</span></span>
        <span class="stat-block__label">escape hatches</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="feature-row__visual">
      <div class="stat-block">
        <span class="stat-block__number"><<span class="stat-block__unit">10</span></span>
        <span class="stat-block__label">milliseconds, incremental</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-row__text">
      <p class="feature-row__num">02 &mdash; Sub-10ms incremental checks</p>
      <h2 class="feature-row__title">Keystroke-responsive.<br>Every edit.</h2>
      <p class="feature-row__body">
        Powered by Salsa &mdash; the same incremental computation framework behind rust-analyzer.
        Basilisk only recomputes what changed. Cold start on 100K LOC in under 5 seconds.
        Keystroke-responsive on every subsequent edit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-row">
    <div class="feature-row__text">
      <p class="feature-row__num">03 &mdash; Ownership semantics</p>
      <h2 class="feature-row__title">Borrow. Mutate.<br>Move. All enforced.</h2>
      <p class="feature-row__body">
        Add <code>Borrowed</code>, <code>InOut</code>, and <code>Owned</code> annotations to express ownership.
        Standard Python syntax &mdash; no compiler required. Catch mutation of borrowed values
        and use-after-move before they reach production.
      </p>
    </div>
